              "oldText": "7.7 If any invoice is not paid within ten days of its due date, Customer shall pay Vendor, as liquidated damages and not as a penalty, an amount equal to fifteen percent of the annual Fees for each week the invoice remains unpaid.",
              "newText": "7.7 If a proper, undisputed invoice is not paid within ten days of its due date, Vendor's sole remedy is simple interest on the overdue amount at the lesser of one percent per month and the maximum rate permitted by Applicable Law, accruing from the due date until paid. No liquidated damages or penalty is payable by Customer under this Agreement."
